# Pull Request Workflow

## Creating a PR

Always target `main` as the base branch. Use `gh pr create`:

```bash
git push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create --title "vX.Y.Z — short description" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary

- bullet 1
- bullet 2
- bullet 3
EOF
)"
```

## PR Body Format

Use a `## Summary` section with bullet points only. No test plan section — CI/CD runs tests automatically on every PR.

```markdown
## Summary

- **`featureX`** — what it does and why
- **API change** — old name → new name, reason
- **Bug fix** — what broke and how it is now fixed
```

## Commit Style

- Imperative mood: `Add`, `Fix`, `Rename`, `Remove`, `Refactor`
- No period at the end
- Keep subject line under 72 characters

```
✅ Add cgroup-aware CPU metrics to /status endpoint
✅ Fix 404 page not respecting language prefix
❌ added some stuff to the status page.
```

## Branch Naming

Use `dev_<target>` or `feature/<short-name>` and always merge into `main`.

## CI/CD

Tests run automatically on every PR — never add a manual test plan to the PR body.
